  "plain": "The book Behind the Flying Saucers tells of a mysterious scientist it calls Dr. G, and the researcher Scott Ramsey says he and his team traced nine real scientists behind that figure to the network of the wartime science chief Vannevar Bush, whose Office of Scientific Research and Development, or OSRD, ran American war research in World War II. Ramsey says that when they went through Bush's group division by division, they found names such as Richard C. Tolman, John Torrance Tate and the Texas Instruments men Cecil Howard Green and Eugene McDermott. If he is right, the people behind an early flying saucer story were wartime science insiders."
